Fixed date-times with a ``TZID`` that names a time zone equivalent to UTC, such as ``Etc/UTC`` or ``Africa/Abidjan``, being written with both the ``TZID`` and a ``Z`` suffix, which :rfc:`5545#section-3.3.5` forbids. This was a regression in 6.1.3. In iCalendar, jCal and xCal output, another name for UTC, such as ``Etc/UTC`` or ``GMT``, is now written in UTC, without the ``TZID``. A place that uses UTC, such as ``Africa/Abidjan`` or ``Atlantic/Reykjavik``, is now treated like any other time zone, as before 6.1.0: it keeps its ``TZID``, also for date-times created in Python, as its rules may change. :meth:`Calendar.add_missing_timezones <icalendar.cal.calendar.Calendar.add_missing_timezones>` adds its ``VTIMEZONE``. I used Claude Opus 5.5 to bisect the regression, write the tests and the fix. @tobixen
